[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'My name is Nick and I am with Classic EV Conversions. And here today I am sat in the world\'s second ever Tesla swap Pontiac Fiero and I\'m going to give you kind of a build breakdown on how this thing kind of works and how it\'s'

[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'together. And I know I said it\'s the second. Believe it or not, it actually is. We built the first Tesla swap Pontiac Vero a number of years ago now. And we had a customer reach out to us and was like, "Hey, can you do that to'

[00:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'mine?" and we happily obliged. So when he came out, we\'re like, "All right, how can we improve on our first build?" And that is exactly what we did. And I\'m going to show you everything we did to make this one better than the first. So'

[00:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'starting with the outside here, it is the all original factory paint job. Our good friend Kurt at Mobile Autodetailing came out, did a two or three stage paint correction on this guy, and also did a'

[00:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'full ceramic coat. So, this car is beautiful and it\'s also super easy to wash. So, I\'m gonna take you from the front here and we\'ll go through the entire system all the way to the back to give you an idea of kind of how it'

[01:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'really works having a Tesla swapped car to be honest. So, right here at the very very nose, and when I mean nose, it\'s just right behind that plastic. We have two Mishimoto radiators. We have one to'

[01:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'keep the motor and the inverter cool, so the motor is nice and happy. And then the other one to keep the batteries cool. On a traditional Tesla, they use freon chillers with AC condensers and'

[01:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'everything like that. For our application here, uh we didn\'t have the need for that. So, we stuck with normal radiators with fans that come on and off. Pumps come on and off at different temperatures to cool heat, kind of keep the batteries right at the happy spot.'

[01:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So, coming up here, kept the factory pop-up headlights. We did put LEDs in it. Uh, anybody that has an old car will know it\'s just terrible driving at night with factory headlights. So, up here we'

[01:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'have five Tesla Model S modules and all the modules in this car are 5.3 kilowatt modules. Also, up here we have a electric hydraulic brake booster. And'

[02:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the reason we use the hydraulic brake booster is a lot of times people will put on kind of vacuum pumps, but when you turn the car on the entire time the'

[02:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'car is running, you just hear a little or like a pump in the background at all times. Using the hydraulic brake booster, what it does is it will pump up to about 2,000 PSI of pressure. And then'

[02:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'as you use up that pressure, it will fill itself back up and then shut back off, which is a really nice feature. And it kind of just keeps the EV quiet cuz it is an electric vehicle, which is really nice. Coming on to the interior'

[02:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'here, I\'ll open this door for you. Come around to the other side. If you look in there, it pretty much looks like a factory 88 Pontiac Fiero. Uh we of course took out the shift knob.'

[02:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Once the shift knob was removed, we replaced that with a just a giant cup holder. These cars are known not to have cup holders at all. We upgraded to a full radio with a display so he can use'

[03:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Android Auto for maps as he\'s going to be driving this car almost daily now that it\'s an EV. Um, when it comes to heat and AC, we don\'t have AC in this build. We do have heat, however,'

[03:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'especially since we live in Colorado. And having the extra batteries in this car makes it handle great in snow, surprisingly. Moving over to the gauges, uh, this customer opted to go all analog. So, we have custom analog gauges'

[03:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'put in the factory gauge cluster. So, it kind of just looks like it\'s supposed to belong there. We got the three gauge pod up here. We have speed, motor temp, battery temp, amps, and we also have our'

[03:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'state of charge. So, our battery level, our high voltage battery, and our low volt standard 12volt battery over here as well. And that\'s kind of it on the inside. Coming around to the back here, this is'

[04:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'where it gets a lot of fun. And it was like playing Tetris. Hold on, I need the key apparently. Let me grab this real quick. Ah. [laughter] All righty. Sorry about that. We'

[04:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'actually just had to get the key replaced on this guy. It was so worn down that you would put it in the ignition and it would practically fall right out. So, back here we have the other 11 Tesla modules, giving us a'

[04:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'total of 16 modules in an 85 kW battery pack. The modules are positioned kind of in like a staircase style right over the Tesla Model S rear drive unit that puts'

[04:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'out almost 400 horsepower. Uh, a few other things to note is we have a Tesla DC toDC under this vent. So, practically your alternator that you would have in a'

[04:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'gas car, but for EVs. So, whenever you turn this guy on, it always holds the voltage at right about 14 volts and can drive with that. Uh, one thing we always joke about with EV conversions or any EVs in general is if your battery ever'

[05:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'die, ever dies, your 12volt battery that ever dies, you can jump start this car enough just to turn the key on, then the high voltage pack and the DC toDC will just keep them running, which is really cool. Um, down here in the trunk, one'

[05:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'thing that we did really different on this build is, as you can tell, there\'s nothing in here. We just have a onboard um not onboard, apologies, a wall charger right here. Beneath this guy'

[05:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'under here, this is actually a false floor and we have dual Elcon 6.6 kW chargers that work together. Uh you might be able to see them, the fans kind'

[05:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of sticking out right under there. So, those are plumbed to the bottom of the trunk with a false floor all sealed in a carpet right on top of that. And our biggest goal with that was on the previous build, we had a high voltage'

[06:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'junction box in the trunk and it took up a lot of space and we just wanted to make this car much more usable, especially from a daily drive perspective. So, putting the chargers under there allowed us to free up almost'

[06:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'all the trunk space. We removed about 3 in from the bottom of the trunk. And in reality, the bottom of the trunk kind of went down to a point, so you couldn\'t really store much down there. Uh when it'

[06:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'comes to the actual charge socket itself, um we opted to use a J1772 charge port on this build, mainly just because it fits well. The customer will mainly charge at J1772 charger stations'

[06:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and at home. Uh we could put a Tesla charger in here, but he didn\'t want to carry around adapter for J1772, and we opted just to go that way. Uh, coming down to the rear here, we are sitting on'

[06:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'factory wheels and tires, but we have upgraded coilovers to support the extra weight in the back. This build came out to be about 600 lb heavier overall. Uh, the weight balance is much more balanced'

[07:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'than factory. So, originally you had the motor in the back, the gas tank in the center, and then the only thing that you have up front is just your spare tire and your radiator. Now having five modules up there, 11 in the back with'

[07:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the motor in the back as well, it is way more balanced. It\'s like a go-kart on rails at this point with how balanced it is and is really, really nice. So, how about we hop in? We\'ll go for a spin and'

[07:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'show you what it\'s like to drive this car. I\'m going to close all this up and then we can go on in. One of the probably coolest things about this is nobody ever expects a Fiero to'

[07:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'be electric. So, our customer likes going to a lot of car shows and what he\'ll do is pull up and everyone\'s just like, "Oh, it\'s a Fiero." and kind of'

[07:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'not think anything else of it. But whenever you roll in and it\'s not making any sound whatsoever and you start opening things up, it definitely draws a crowd, which is really cool.'

[08:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So, like any other car, key in, turn it on, the gauges will do their opening ceremony. Everything will turn on as it should should. And then safety first as always. And it\'s a pretty hot day today,'

[08:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'so you can hear the fans just turned on. Um, and that is to keep the batteries and the motor in the ideal temperature range. So, pretty much to drive you just press'

[08:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the brake, turn the shift knob to drive, make sure the e bra and everything is off and from there you just press the gas and go and we are off. It is honestly a very very smooth'

[08:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'driving car with everything from single pedal driving to almost no regen. You can adjust the regen exactly exactly how you like. Um we find this car gets about'

[09:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '230 mi of range given on how you drive it and everything like that. We\'ll go over here and I\'ll I\'ll pull off for you a little bit. Woohoo!'

[09:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Man, does this thing go. Ah, so our Fiero is currently out of commission uh due to a radiator needing to be replaced. And just having this car done'

[09:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and on the road has motivated us to get our Fiero back together. But h when it comes to driving this thing, it is so smooth, so simple. You don\'t need any maintenance. And yeah, if you just'

[09:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'change brakes here and there, then it\'s it. It\'s great to go. [snorts]'

